  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A metal chloride contains <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>55</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>%</mo></math> of chlorine by weight. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mL</mi></math> vapours of the metal chloride at STP weigh <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>57</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math>. The molecular formula of the metal chloride is</p><p>(Given: Atomic mass of chlorine is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>35</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">u</mi></math>)</p>"
  },
